      "description": "Watches Claude Code sessions through its hooks and lets you approve or reject permission requests from the pads. Sessions appear when their first hook fires.",
      "detail": "Turn on the local hook endpoint in Agents > Adapters.",
      "diagnostics": [],
      "id": "claude-code",
      "kind": "hooks",
      "limits": [
        "Hooks observe and can answer permission requests. They cannot pause, resume, cancel, retry or instruct a running session, so those controls stay unavailable.",
        "You can answer from LaunchDeck only if control was granted before the request arrived; otherwise Claude Code asks you in its own prompt.",
        "A held request falls back to Claude Code's own prompt after the hold time. Nothing is ever approved on your behalf.",
        "A turn that ends in an API error is shown as failed; failures inside a tool call are not.",
        "Sessions that started before the hooks were configured show up at their next event.",
        "Checked against Claude Code 2.1.289 (2026-10-04)."
      ],
      "name": "Claude Code (hooks)",
      "state": "disabled"
    },
