      "diagnostics": [],
      "id": "codex",
      "kind": "hooks",
      "limits": [
        "Hooks observe and can answer permission requests. They cannot pause, resume, cancel, retry or instruct a running session, so those controls stay unavailable.",
        "You can answer from LaunchDeck only if control was granted before the request arrived; otherwise Codex asks you in its own prompt.",
        "A held request falls back to Codex's own prompt after the hold time. Nothing is ever approved on your behalf.",
        "Written from OpenAI's published hook documentation (2026-10-04) and not yet run against a Codex installation: treat it as untested.",
        "Codex's app-server protocol would allow real control (start, interrupt, steer); it is not implemented here.",
        "The relay uses curl and an sh-compatible shell."
      ],
      "name": "Codex (hooks)",
      "state": "disabled"
